; exit 77 (see .exit)
;
; `vecPop` REFUSES an empty vector: `464-index-trap.ax`'s decision,
; applied to the second accessor that carried a sentinel.
;
; WHY THE COVERAGE MOVED HERE. `vecPop`'s body answered `0` on an empty
; vector, and under `(-> (Vec a) a)` that `0` FABRICATES an `a` -
; exactly what `vecGet`'s out-of-range sentinel did before it was made
; to trap. `docs/generics-design.md` section 4 records the decision for
; `vecGet`, and the paragraph that follows it ("`vecPop` is a second
; `vecGet`, and section 4 did not name it") records this one. A caller
; who does not know the vector is non-empty bounds the walk by
; `vecLen`, which is what `vecGet`'s own comment says of the same
; question, or reads through `vecTry` and gets a `None`.
;
; `070-vec.ax` carried the over-pop terms until the trap landed, in two
; places - a pop of the fresh vector, printed at line 4 of its 47-line
; golden, and two surplus pops in `popTimes`. It can carry neither now,
; because a program that over-pops cannot also print the 43 lines that
; stood after the first. So the over-pop is a case of its own, its walk
; there is bounded to the elements that exist, and what stands here
; ASSERTS the refusal instead of printing a fabricated zero.
;
; THE LEGAL HALF IS HERE TOO, because a trap is only worth having if it
; fires on nothing else. A vector that HAS elements pops them last-in
; first-out and its length falls by one each time, printed element by
; element rather than as a summary so that a pop answering the wrong
; slot is visible and not merely miscounted. The checked read on the
; emptied vector answers `None` and does not trap: refusing is
; `vecPop`'s answer, not `Vec`'s.
;
; The status is in `465-pop-empty-trap.exit`, the sentence in `.err`,
; and neither checks the other: a program that printed the right
; sentence and exited 0 fails on the status, and one that exited 77 in
; silence fails on the stderr.
(import IO)

(import Vec)

(import Str)

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  ; --- LEGAL: three elements, popped LIFO, the length falling ---
  (let ((v vecNew))
    {
      (vecPush v 7)
      (vecPush v 8)
      (vecPush v 9)
      (println (vecLen v))  ; 3
      (println
        (cast Int (vecPop v))
      )
      ; 9: last in, first out
      (println (vecLen v))  ; 2
      (println
        (cast Int (vecPop v))
      )
      ; 8
      (println
        (cast Int (vecPop v))
      )
      ; 7
      (println (vecLen v))  ; 0: popped exactly to empty, never negative
      ; --- LEGAL: the checked read a caller writes instead ---
      (println
        (match (vecTry v 0)
          ((Some x) x)
          ((None) (- 0 1))
        )
      )
      ; -1: None, and no trap - the refusal is `vecPop`'s
      ; --- ILLEGAL: one pop past empty, and this is where it ends ---
      (println
        (cast Int (vecPop v))
      )
      ; NOT REACHED, and deliberately not a bare numeral:
      ; `verify-stdlib-out.py` models a case's exit status from `main`'s
      ; tail when that tail is one, and this program's status comes from
      ; the trap rather than from its last expression. It is also the
      ; tripwire for the trap being removed - if `vecPop` ever starts
      ; answering 0 again, this line runs and the golden says so.
      (printlnLit (strCStr "UNREACHABLE: the empty pop returned"))
    }
  )
)
